oth curve near the top. The trunk is not wavy.", "render-2 (seed 1, P-TRUNK): the crown seen closer. The fronds droop and have lanceolate leaflets. The trunk is smooth dark brown with small, widely spaced knobs.", "render-3 (seed 1, P-BASE): the metadata marks visibility as hidden. The frame shows a close, smooth trunk surface with about four cone-shaped stubs and no diamond pattern.", "reference-0: a strongly leaning, S-curved date palm with a large, dense crown of long fronds, a dead-frond skirt and orange fruit clusters. reference-1 and reference-2: an upright trunk covered in a dense diamond pattern of leaf bases with fibrous matting and ferns growing on it.", "The finish of the renders is at or above the finish of the spruce anchor (anchor-0). Only finish is compared to the anchor, not morphology."], "findings": [{"observation": "Both seeds show a crown that reads as a palm rosette of pinnate fronds, with the lowest fronds drooping. Compared with reference-0, the fronds are short relative to the trunk and there are far fewer of them.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The settings for frond length and frond count may still be too low. This is a guess from the images and was not checked."}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight (seed 1) or gently leaning (seed 42), with a near-constant diameter and no waviness.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk. The only things on it are small leaf-base stubs, which belong to the palm; there are no ferns, branches or leaves.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Where drawn, the trunk is smooth, with sparse knobs instead of the dense spiral diamond pattern of l